  "description_html": "Skeletal composite of the known and unknown material of Pellegrinisaurus, based on the holotype MPCA 1500 (About 20-25 meters long). The holotype is represented by 4 dorsal and 26 caudal vertebrae, and a partial right femur, although there is only one dorsal figured in the paper, the other three dorsals were made in reference to the figured one.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The right femur is depicted in a lateral view, based on <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.skeletaldrawing.com/sauropods-and-kin/futalognkosaurus\">Scott Hartman's Futalognkosaurus</a> since the paper lacks a lateral one. The silhouette is based on the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.skeletaldrawing.com/sauropods-and-kin/alamosaurus\">Scott Hartman's Alamosaurus</a>. Frutalognkosaurus and Alamosaurus were used as references since they are found to be relatives of Pellegrinisaurus in most cladistic analysis.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Bandeira2016_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Bandeira2016-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Color_Key\">Color Key</h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FFFFFF\" title=\"#FFFFFF\"> </b> Known</li>\n<li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#777777\" title=\"#777777\"> </b> Unknown</li></ul>",
